## Slot vocabulary ({{slot-count}} slots inherited or declared)

Organization memorials inherit `:mm/Memory` plus type-specific slots:

- **`org-class`** (required) — `company` / `community` / `project` / `research-partnership`
- **`members`** — list of actor rel-paths (inverse of `belongs-to:`)
- **`founded`** — date or descriptive
- **`url`** — primary external URL

{{slot-table}}

## Org-class vocabulary

- **`company`** — for-profit entity (employer, AI provider, consulting client)
- **`community`** — open-source community, research community, professional society
- **`project`** — bounded collaboration with defined scope and lifetime
- **`research-partnership`** — formal cross-organization research collaboration

## Canonical body structure

```markdown
## What this organization is

<Type of organization, founding context, primary purpose.>

## Notable members

<Actor cross-references; humans + AI models the organization
includes.>

## Relationship to the corpus

<How the corpus author engages with this organization;
authoritative pronouncements that bind the corpus; references
the corpus cites.>

## See also

<Adjacent organizations, member actors, relevant references.>
```

## Composition with adjacent classes

- **`actor`** — actors `belongs-to` organizations (many-to-many)
- **`authorization`** — authorizations may originate from organizational authority (e.g., license grants)
- **`reference`** — official documentation from an organization is typically a reference; the organization is cited as `created-by:`

